From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Sat, 03 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman_pcd: revive ehash+inline-opcode VLAN (T-M6-8d), align with vendor fill_actions()

Today's deep review of the vendor SDK that's actually proven to sustain
VLAN on this silicon (/mnt/builds/ASK, cdx/cmm/dpa_app, the stack
running on .116) found that "Option A" (CC-leaf AD -> NADEN -> VLAN
HMTD, ASK2-VLAN-REARCH.md, shipped 2026-08-26) is architecturally
foreign to what vendor actually does:

- Vendor's own declarative FMC policy (dpa_app/files/etc/cdx_pcd.xml,
  525 lines, read in full) declares EVERY ONE of its 16 classification
  nodes -- TCP4/UDP4/TCP6/UDP6/ESP4/ESP6/multicast/the L2 bridge
  table/PPPoE/3-tuple/fragmentation, on every port including both
  OFFLINE ports -- as <hashtable external="yes" .../>. There is no
  RM-style CC match-table classification node anywhere in vendor's
  shipped configuration, for any traffic class, on any port.
- Reading cdx_ehash.c directly: routed VLAN pop/push (fill_actions(),
  the function that handles routed TCP/UDP, as opposed to the
  MAC-keyed fill_bridge_actions() used only for pure L2 switching) is
  just more inline FE-VM opcodes (STRIP_ALL_VLAN 0x12 / INSERT_VLAN_HDR
  0x42) in the SAME per-flow ehash record that handles routing/NAT.
  No OH-port, no NADEN, no HMTD anywhere in vendor's routed-VLAN path.
- Separately, today's own board A/B testing (patch 0209 attempt #1,
  commit b72338d2, reverted) and a six-weeks-earlier investigation
  (plans/CC-TREE-REBUILD-PLAN.md, 2026-08-05 FINAL VERDICT) both
  independently found that reaching AC_CC dispatch via next_engine=3
  reliably wedges this silicon (RX-deaf, cold-boot-only recovery),
  while next_engine=2 is safe but always "dual delivers" (a real HW
  classification AND a simultaneous software-path copy, capping
  throughput). Vendor's own kgse_ccbs=0 on a working scheme (recorded
  in arch/fman-microcode-210-programming-reference.md) suggests vendor
  never reaches this register at all for ordinary classification.

So Option A swapped a narrowly-buggy-but-correct mechanism (the
original F-233/0174 inline-opcode path, retired 2026-08-26 after
freezing at ~21 packets, a per-task FE-VM management-index resource
exhaustion that was never root-caused) for an architecturally-foreign
one that vendor doesn't use for this purpose at all -- which is very
plausibly why Option A has itself been fragile (dual delivery / wedge,
confirmed today).

This patch re-adds VLAN opcode emission to fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(),
matching vendor's fill_actions() order exactly: STRIP_ALL_VLAN (0x12,
mandatory-first on POP, real ingress VID + op_flags=0/VALIDATE, per
vendor's "strip vlan hdrs is called mandatorily to validate the vlan
id's" comment) -> TTL/HOPLIMIT or fused NAT (unchanged existing logic)
-> INSERT_VLAN_HDR (0x42, single tag, control word (num_hdrs=1)<<24 +
one (TCI<<16)|inner-EtherType word, PUSH only) -> INSERT_L2_HDR (now
embedding the VLAN TPID as the new outer ethertype when PUSH is active,
instead of the original inner ethertype) -> ENQUEUE_PKT.

Byte-identical to the current (post-F-233-retirement) record whenever
the new optional `vlan` parameter is NULL or vlan->flags==0 -- verified
by inspection: every new code path is gated on vlan/vlan->flags and
every existing oi/l2poff/param_off computation is threaded through an
intermediate (ttl_param_off) that equals the old hardcoded param_off
in the no-VLAN case.

This does NOT yet fix the original ~21-packet freeze (that mechanism-
level bug, most likely INSERT_VLAN_HDR's internal checksum/DMA
submission asymmetry per the 2026-09-10 microcode disassembly, is
still uncharacterized) -- it re-establishes the vendor-aligned
mechanism and is the necessary first step before that bug can be
chased on the right substrate. ask.ko (board-tracked, not behind this
patch) is wired in a companion change to call this path for VLAN flows
instead of the CC-tree path; ask_vlan_cc.c is left in place, unused,
as an easy revert if this does not pan out.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: B (re-adds previously-
shipped-then-retired inline-opcode emission to an existing, heavily
proven function; gated so the no-VLAN record path is byte-identical;
known failure mode if the old freeze recurs is a clean stall after
~21 packets, not a wedge/crash, per the extensive prior P0 campaign)
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
index 36ee7220f7ac..2fdf15651510 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -2252,24 +2252,29 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 				  u32 enq_off, u32 fqid, bool stats,
 				  const u8 *l2_dst, const u8 *l2_src,
 				  u16 eth_type,
-				  const struct fman_pcd_nat_params *nat);
-/* F-230: debugfs fe_flow add path never performs NAT. */
+				  const struct fman_pcd_nat_params *nat,
+				  const struct fman_pcd_vlan_params *vlan);
+/* F-230: debugfs fe_flow add path never performs NAT; T-M6-8d adds an
+ * optional vlan param so the debug harness can de-risk the revived
+ * inline-opcode VLAN path independently of ask.ko. */
 static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key_natwrap_dbgfs(
 				  struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 				  const u8 *key, u8 key_size,
 				  u32 enq_off, u32 fqid, bool stats,
 				  const u8 *l2_dst, const u8 *l2_src,
-				  u16 eth_type)
+				  u16 eth_type,
+				  const struct fman_pcd_vlan_params *vlan)
 {
 	return fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(t, key, key_size, enq_off, fqid, stats,
-				      l2_dst, l2_src, eth_type, NULL);
+				      l2_dst, l2_src, eth_type, NULL, vlan);
 }
 static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 				  const u8 *key, u8 key_size,
 				  u32 enq_off, u32 fqid, bool stats,
 				  const u8 *l2_dst, const u8 *l2_src,
 				  u16 eth_type,
-				  const struct fman_pcd_nat_params *nat)
+				  const struct fman_pcd_nat_params *nat,
+				  const struct fman_pcd_vlan_params *vlan)
 {
 	struct fman_pcd_ehash_flow *flow;
 	u64 prev_head, old_native, rec_phys;
@@ -2306,6 +2311,8 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 	/* F-198 (T-M7-2 S1): vendor ordered opcode/parameter record. */
 	#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_ENQUEUE_PKT		0x01
 	#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_INSERT_L2_HDR	0x41
+	#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_STRIP_ALL_VLAN	0x12
+	#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_INSERT_VLAN_HDR	0x42
 	{
 		size_t opc_off = FMAN_EHASH_FLOW_KEY_OFF + ALIGN(key_size, sizeof(u32));
 		size_t param_off = opc_off + 16;	/* MAX_OPCODES */
@@ -2334,14 +2341,43 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 			 * payload needs two pad bytes, so word = 14 | (2 << 29) =
 			 * 0x4000000e. L2 param consumes 20B. */
 			#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_UPDATE_TTL	0x21
-			size_t l2poff = param_off;
+			size_t ttl_param_off = param_off;
+			size_t l2poff;
 			size_t oi = 0;
+			u16 l2_eth_type = eth_type;
+			bool vlan_pop = vlan && (vlan->flags & FMAN_PCD_VLANF_POP);
+
+			/* T-M6-8d (ehash-vlan-revival): STRIP_ALL_VLAN (0x12) is
+			 * vendor's mandatory-first opcode for a routed POP -- see
+			 * fill_actions()'s "strip vlan hdrs is called mandatorily
+			 * to validate the vlan id's" comment. Vendor writes the
+			 * real ingress VID (en_ehash_strip_all_vlan_hdrs: BE
+			 * vlan_id[2] outer-first, a 4B validating word, op_flags,
+			 * 12B total) and leaves op_flags=0 (VALIDATE) for a routed
+			 * tagged POP -- OP_SKIP_VLAN_VALIDATE is a bridge-only case
+			 * this ehash path never takes. Must run before the TTL/NAT
+			 * opcode so later params land after it; ttl_param_off (not
+			 * param_off) is threaded through so the no-VLAN case stays
+			 * byte-identical. */
+			if (vlan_pop) {
+				r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_STRIP_ALL_VLAN;
+				*(__be16 *)(r + param_off + 0) =
+					cpu_to_be16(vlan->ingress_vid);
+				*(__be16 *)(r + param_off + 2) = cpu_to_be16(0);
+				*(__be32 *)(r + param_off + 4) = cpu_to_be32(0);
+				*(r + param_off + 8) = 0;	/* op_flags = VALIDATE */
+				*(r + param_off + 9) = 0;
+				*(r + param_off + 10) = 0;
+				*(r + param_off + 11) = 0;
+				ttl_param_off = param_off + 12;
+			}
+			l2poff = ttl_param_off;
 
 			if (eth_type == 0x0800) {
 				/* UPDATE_TTL opcode + 4B zero DSCP param first. */
 				r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_UPDATE_TTL;
-				*(__be32 *)(r + param_off + 0) = cpu_to_be32(0);
-				l2poff = param_off + 4;
+				*(__be32 *)(r + ttl_param_off + 0) = cpu_to_be32(0);
+				l2poff = ttl_param_off + 4;
 			} else if (eth_type == 0x86dd) {
 				/* F-226(hoplimit): IPv6 hop-limit decrement, the v6
 				 * counterpart of UPDATE_TTL (vendor fm_ehash.h
@@ -2350,8 +2386,8 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 				 * decrement the hop limit on forward. */
 				#define FMAN_EHASH_OPC_UPDATE_HOPLIMIT	0x29
 				r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_UPDATE_HOPLIMIT;
-				*(__be32 *)(r + param_off + 0) = cpu_to_be32(0);
-				l2poff = param_off + 4;
+				*(__be32 *)(r + ttl_param_off + 0) = cpu_to_be32(0);
+				l2poff = ttl_param_off + 4;
 			}
 			/* F-230 (T-M6-7.1): vendor create_nat_hm encoding.
 			 * NAT opcodes are BIT-FUSED (OR'd into one byte per operation
@@ -2373,11 +2409,14 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 				u8 l3_opc;
 				bool pv6 = nat->is_v6;
 
-				/* Rebuild the opcode list + params from param_off in the
-				 * vendor NAT order. The no-NAT branch below never executes
-				 * this reset, preserving F-200/F-226 byte identity. */
-				oi = 0;
-				l2poff = param_off;
+				/* Rebuild the opcode list + params from ttl_param_off
+				 * (after any STRIP_ALL_VLAN prefix) in the vendor NAT
+				 * order. The no-NAT branch above never executes this
+				 * reset, preserving F-200/F-226 byte identity; a VLAN
+				 * prefix (if any) is preserved since oi/l2poff reset
+				 * relative to ttl_param_off, not param_off. */
+				oi = vlan_pop ? 1 : 0;
+				l2poff = ttl_param_off;
 				if (nat->flags & FMAN_PCD_NATF_SPAT)
 					port_opc |= FMAN_EHASH_OPC_UPDATE_SPORT;
 				if (nat->flags & FMAN_PCD_NATF_DPAT)
@@ -2411,12 +2450,28 @@ static int fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(struct fman_pcd_ehash_table *t,
 					l2poff += pv6 ? 16 : 4;
 				}
 			}
+			/* T-M6-8d: INSERT_VLAN_HDR (0x42) runs after TTL/NAT, just
+			 * before the L2 rebuild -- vendor create_vlan_ins_hm(), a
+			 * single-tag en_ehash_insert_vlan_hdr: control word
+			 * (num_hdrs=1)<<24, then one (TCI<<16)|inner-EtherType word.
+			 * The frame's new OUTER ethertype becomes the VLAN TPID, so
+			 * the INSERT_L2_HDR param below must embed push_tpid, not
+			 * the original (inner) eth_type. */
+			if (vlan && (vlan->flags & FMAN_PCD_VLANF_PUSH)) {
+				r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_INSERT_VLAN_HDR;
+				*(__be32 *)(r + l2poff + 0) = cpu_to_be32(1u << 24);
+				*(__be32 *)(r + l2poff + 4) =
+					cpu_to_be32(((u32)vlan->push_tci << 16) |
+						    eth_type);
+				l2poff += 8;
+				l2_eth_type = vlan->push_tpid;
+			}
 			r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_INSERT_L2_HDR;
 			r[opc_off + oi++] = FMAN_EHASH_OPC_ENQUEUE_PKT;
 			*(__be32 *)(r + l2poff + 0) = cpu_to_be32(0x4000000e);
 			memcpy(r + l2poff + 4, l2_dst, 6);
 			memcpy(r + l2poff + 10, l2_src, 6);
-			*(__be16 *)(r + l2poff + 16) = cpu_to_be16(eth_type);
+			*(__be16 *)(r + l2poff + 16) = cpu_to_be16(l2_eth_type);
 			enqueue_off = l2poff + 20;	/* after L2 (ALIGN(4+14,4)) */
 		} else {
 			/* Byte-identical F-197 RX-reinjection terminal. */
@@ -2937,7 +2992,7 @@ static ssize_t fman_pcd_fe_flow_write(struct file *file,
 	err = fman_pcd_ehash_add_key_natwrap_dbgfs(t, key, key_size,
 				     drop ? (u32)pcd->fe_exit_off :
 					    (u32)enq_obj->muram_off, (u32)fqid,
-				     stats, NULL, NULL, 0);
+				     stats, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL);
 
 	if (!err) {
 		/* F-177 (T-M3-R Phase 2 item 2): assert FMFP_EXTC[INV0] SYNC
@@ -5117,6 +5172,12 @@ int fman_pcd_fe_flow_add(struct fman *fm, u8 hw_port_id,
 			.sport  = action->nat_sport,
 			.dport  = action->nat_dport,
 		};
+		struct fman_pcd_vlan_params _vlan = {
+			.flags     = action->vlan_flags,
+			.ingress_vid = action->vlan_ingress_vid,
+			.push_tci  = action->vlan_push_tci,
+			.push_tpid = action->vlan_push_tpid,
+		};
 		int err;
 
 		memcpy(_nat.sip, action->nat_sip, 16);
@@ -5139,7 +5200,8 @@ int fman_pcd_fe_flow_add(struct fman *fm, u8 hw_port_id,
 						 (u32)rec_ctx, hit_fqid,
 						 false /* F-189(genl-stats-false) */,
 						 l2_dst, l2_src, l2_eth,
-						 &_nat);
+						 &_nat,
+						 action->vlan_flags ? &_vlan : NULL);
 
 	if (!err) {
 		/* F-177 (T-M3-R Phase 2 item 2): assert FMFP_EXTC[INV0] SYNC
diff --git a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
index 171b8e3f7c2c..c0daa51ffe0d 100644
--- a/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
+++ b/include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h
@@ -441,6 +441,27 @@ struct fman_pcd_fe_flow_action {
 	u8   nat_dip[16];
 	__be16 nat_sport;
 	__be16 nat_dport;
+	/* T-M6-8d (ehash-vlan-revival): VLAN pop/push, vendor fill_actions()
+	 * mechanism (inline FE-VM opcodes in the same ehash record used for
+	 * routing/NAT) instead of the CC-tree+NADEN+HMTD path. vlan_flags==0
+	 * => no VLAN edit (record byte-identical to the plain routed path). */
+	u8   vlan_flags;
+	u16  vlan_ingress_vid;	/* host order; STRIP_ALL_VLAN validation */
+	u16  vlan_push_tci;	/* host order; PCP<<13|DEI<<12|VID */
+	u16  vlan_push_tpid;	/* host order; outer EtherType, e.g. 0x8100 */
+};
+
+/* T-M6-8d: vlan_flags bits, mirroring ask.ko's ASK_VLANF_*. */
+#define FMAN_PCD_VLANF_POP	(1u << 0)
+#define FMAN_PCD_VLANF_PUSH	(1u << 1)
+
+/* VLAN rewrite parameters threaded into the ehash record emitter, the
+ * vlan-equivalent of struct fman_pcd_nat_params below. */
+struct fman_pcd_vlan_params {
+	u8  flags;		/* FMAN_PCD_VLANF_* */
+	u16 ingress_vid;
+	u16 push_tci;
+	u16 push_tpid;
 };
 
 /* F-230: NAT rewrite parameters threaded into the ehash record emitter.
